    <dcterms:title>The Master of Ballantrae: A Winter's Tale</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Master_of_Ballantrae</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>David Price</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"The Master of Ballantrae: A Winter's Tale" by Robert Louis Stevenson is a novel published in 1889. Two Scottish brothers find their family torn apart when the Jacobite rising of 1745 forces them to choose opposite sides in the conflict. When the rebellious elder brother is reported dead, the younger inherits everything—until a messenger arrives years later with shocking news. What follows is a dark tale of rivalry, betrayal, and obsession that spans from the Scottish highlands to pirate ships and the American wilderness. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 76.2 (7th grade). Fairly easy to read.</pgterms:marc908>
